Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• gameId: unique identifier used to link a pitch to the game and – if needed – to the `schedules` table for auxiliary game data.  
• seasonType / year: let you separate or merge regular‑season (`REG`) and post‑season (`PST`) records.  
• pitcherId: the player we are looking for; use to group, filter and compare pitch speeds.  
• pitcherFirstName / pitcherLastName: retrieve the pitcher’s full name once the right pitcherId is found.  
• pitchSpeed: numeric value to be maximised (ignore 0 or NULL).  
• homeTeamId / awayTeamId and homeTeamName / awayTeamName: candidate team to which a pitcher could belong in that row.  
• awayFielder1‑12, awayBatter1‑9, homeFielder1‑12, homeBatter1‑9 (and/or lineupTeamId / lineupPlayerId): confirm that the pitcherId really appears on the appropriate team’s roster for that game.  
• is_wild_pitch, is_bunt, etc.: not needed for the requested task but available for deeper filtering if desired.  

Typical conditions that may be useful  
• pitchSpeed > 0                      – to eliminate invalid speeds  
• pitcherId IS NOT NULL              – only real pitchers  
• seasonType IN ('REG','PST')        – combine regular and post‑season  
• pitcherId IN UNNEST(array_of_team_players) – validate the pitcher actually appears in the home/away lists for that game  

Below are ten exploratory BigQuery SQL snippets – from very simple inspections to more involved checks – each capped at 20 rows so you can quickly view sample data.  
Remember to run them in the public project `bigquery-public-data.baseball`.

```sql
-- Description: 1) Peek at a few regular‑season pitch events with non‑zero pitch speed.
SELECT gameId, year, pitchSpeed, pitcherId, pitcherFirstName, pitcherLastName
FROM `bigquery-public-data.baseball.games_wide`
WHERE pitchSpeed > 0
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 2) Same peek for post‑season games to verify similar structure.
SELECT gameId, year, pitchSpeed, pitcherId, pitcherFirstName, pitcherLastName
FROM `bigquery-public-data.baseball.games_post_wide`
WHERE pitchSpeed > 0
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 3) Highest raw pitch speeds (regular season only), ignoring team logic for now.
SELECT DISTINCT pitcherId, pitchSpeed
FROM `bigquery-public-data.baseball.games_wide`
WHERE pitchSpeed > 0
ORDER BY pitchSpeed DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 4) Highest raw pitch speeds (post‑season only).
SELECT DISTINCT pitcherId, pitchSpeed
FROM `bigquery-public-data.baseball.games_post_wide`
WHERE pitchSpeed > 0
ORDER BY pitchSpeed DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 5) Show a pitcher’s top speed together with name (regular season).
SELECT pitcherId,
       MAX(pitchSpeed) AS max_speed,
       ANY_VALUE(pitcherFirstName) AS first_name,
       ANY_VALUE(pitcherLastName)  AS last_name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.baseball.games_wide`
WHERE pitchSpeed > 0
GROUP BY pitcherId
ORDER BY max_speed DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 6) Build an array of all HOME player IDs then keep only rows
-- where the pitcher is confirmed to be on the home team.
SELECT gameId,
       homeTeamId,
       homeTeamName,
       pitcherId,
       pitchSpeed
FROM `bigquery-public-data.baseball.games_wide`
WHERE pitchSpeed > 0
  AND pitcherId IN UNNEST(ARRAY[
        homeFielder1, homeFielder2, homeFielder3, homeFielder4, homeFielder5, homeFielder6,
        homeFielder7, homeFielder8, homeFielder9, homeFielder10, homeFielder11, homeFielder12,
        homeBatter1,  homeBatter2,  homeBatter3,  homeBatter4,  homeBatter5,
        homeBatter6,  homeBatter7,  homeBatter8,  homeBatter9 ])
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 7) Same logic but for the AWAY side, post‑season table.
SELECT gameId,
       awayTeamId,
       awayTeamName,
       pitcherId,
       pitchSpeed
FROM `bigquery-public-data.baseball.games_post_wide`
WHERE pitchSpeed > 0
  AND pitcherId IN UNNEST(ARRAY[
        awayFielder1, awayFielder2, awayFielder3, awayFielder4, awayFielder5, awayFielder6,
        awayFielder7, awayFielder8, awayFielder9, awayFielder10, awayFielder11, awayFielder12,
        awayBatter1,  awayBatter2,  awayBatter3,  awayBatter4,  awayBatter5,
        awayBatter6,  awayBatter7,  awayBatter8,  awayBatter9 ])
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 8) For each team (regular season), obtain the single highest valid pitch
-- after confirming the pitcher belongs to that team in the given game row.
SELECT t.homeTeamId            AS team_id,
       t.homeTeamName          AS team_name,
       MAX(t.pitchSpeed)       AS max_speed
FROM `bigquery-public-data.baseball.games_wide` AS t
WHERE t.pitchSpeed > 0
  AND t.pitcherId IN UNNEST(ARRAY[
        t.homeFielder1, t.homeFielder2, t.homeFielder3, t.homeFielder4, t.homeFielder5, t.homeFielder6,
        t.homeFielder7, t.homeFielder8, t.homeFielder9, t.homeFielder10, t.homeFielder11, t.homeFielder12,
        t.homeBatter1,  t.homeBatter2,  t.homeBatter3,  t.homeBatter4,  t.homeBatter5,
        t.homeBatter6,  t.homeBatter7,  t.homeBatter8,  t.homeBatter9 ])
GROUP BY team_id, team_name
ORDER BY max_speed DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 9) Same as (8) but combine regular and post‑season via UNION ALL,
-- tagging row_origin so you can see if speeds come from REG or PST.
WITH union_games AS (
  SELECT 'REG' AS row_origin, *
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.baseball.games_wide`
  UNION ALL
  SELECT 'PST' AS row_origin, *
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.baseball.games_post_wide`
)
SELECT row_origin,
       team_id,
       team_name,
       MAX(pitchSpeed) AS max_speed
FROM (
  SELECT row_origin,
         CASE
           WHEN pitcherId IN UNNEST(ARRAY[
                homeFielder1, homeFielder2, homeFielder3, homeFielder4, homeFielder5, homeFielder6,
                homeFielder7, homeFielder8, homeFielder9, homeFielder10, homeFielder11, homeFielder12,
                homeBatter1,  homeBatter2,  homeBatter3,  homeBatter4,  homeBatter5,
                homeBatter6,  homeBatter7,  homeBatter8,  homeBatter9 ])
           THEN homeTeamId
           WHEN pitcherId IN UNNEST(ARRAY[
                awayFielder1, awayFielder2, awayFielder3, awayFielder4, awayFielder5, awayFielder6,
                awayFielder7, awayFielder8, awayFielder9, awayFielder10, awayFielder11, awayFielder12,
                awayBatter1,  awayBatter2,  awayBatter3,  awayBatter4,  awayBatter5,
                awayBatter6,  awayBatter7,  awayBatter8,  awayBatter9 ])
           THEN awayTeamId
         END AS team_id,
         CASE
           WHEN pitcherId IN UNNEST(ARRAY[
                homeFielder1, homeFielder2, homeFielder3, homeFielder4, homeFielder5, homeFielder6,
                homeFielder7, homeFielder8, homeFielder9, homeFielder10, homeFielder11, homeFielder12,
                homeBatter1,  homeBatter2,  homeBatter3,  homeBatter4,  homeBatter5,
                homeBatter6,  homeBatter7,  homeBatter8,  homeBatter9 ])
           THEN homeTeamName
           WHEN pitcherId IN UNNEST(ARRAY[
                awayFielder1, awayFielder2, awayFielder3, awayFielder4, awayFielder5, awayFielder6,
                awayFielder7, awayFielder8, awayFielder9, awayFielder10, awayFielder11, awayFielder12,
                awayBatter1,  awayBatter2,  awayBatter3,  awayBatter4,  awayBatter5,
                awayBatter6,  awayBatter7,  awayBatter8,  awayBatter9 ])
           THEN awayTeamName
         END AS team_name,
         pitchSpeed
  FROM union_games
  WHERE pitchSpeed > 0
)
WHERE team_id IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY row_origin, team_id, team_name
ORDER BY max_speed DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 10) Full answer sketch (still limited to 20 rows) –
-- for each team, grab the pitcher who threw the single highest valid pitch
-- across both seasons and bring back his name.
WITH union_games AS (
  SELECT * FROM `bigquery-public-data.baseball.games_wide`
  UNION ALL
  SELECT * FROM `bigquery-public-data.baseball.games_post_wide`
),
validated AS (
  SELECT
    CASE
      WHEN pitcherId IN UNNEST(ARRAY[
            homeFielder1, homeFielder2, homeFielder3, homeFielder4, homeFielder5, homeFielder6,
            homeFielder7, homeFielder8, homeFielder9, homeFielder10, homeFielder11, homeFielder12,
            homeBatter1,  homeBatter2,  homeBatter3,  homeBatter4,  homeBatter5,
            homeBatter6,  homeBatter7,  homeBatter8,  homeBatter9 ])
      THEN homeTeamId
      WHEN pitcherId IN UNNEST(ARRAY[
            awayFielder1, awayFielder2, awayFielder3, awayFielder4, awayFielder5, awayFielder6,
            awayFielder7, awayFielder8, awayFielder9, awayFielder10, awayFielder11, awayFielder12,
            awayBatter1,  awayBatter2,  awayBatter3,  awayBatter4,  awayBatter5,
            awayBatter6,  awayBatter7,  awayBatter8,  awayBatter9 ])
      THEN awayTeamId
    END AS team_id,
    CASE
      WHEN pitcherId IN UNNEST(ARRAY[
            homeFielder1, homeFielder2, homeFielder3, homeFielder4, homeFielder5, homeFielder6,
            homeFielder7, homeFielder8, homeFielder9, homeFielder10, homeFielder11, homeFielder12,
            homeBatter1,  homeBatter2,  homeBatter3,  homeBatter4,  homeBatter5,
            homeBatter6,  homeBatter7,  homeBatter8,  homeBatter9 ])
      THEN homeTeamName
      WHEN pitcherId IN UNNEST(ARRAY[
            awayFielder1, awayFielder2, awayFielder3, awayFielder4, awayFielder5, awayFielder6,
            awayFielder7, awayFielder8, awayFielder9, awayFielder10, awayFielder11, awayFielder12,
            awayBatter1,  awayBatter2,  awayBatter3,  awayBatter4,  awayBatter5,
            awayBatter6,  awayBatter7,  awayBatter8,  awayBatter9 ])
      THEN awayTeamName
    END AS team_name,
    pitcherId,
    CONCAT(pitcherFirstName, ' ', pitcherLastName) AS pitcher_full_name,
    pitchSpeed
  FROM union_games
  WHERE pitchSpeed > 0
)
SELECT team_name,
       pitcher_full_name,
       MAX(pitchSpeed) AS team_top_speed
FROM validated
WHERE team_id IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY team_name, pitcher_full_name
ORDER BY team_top_speed DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

Each step lets you inspect the data and progressively build toward the final requirement: “the pitcher who achieved the highest non‑zero pitch speed for each team, validated by roster presence, together with that speed.”
